1
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:06,506
Why...

2
00:00:06,507 --> 00:00:08,508
Why do you look like... me?

3
00:00:08,509 --> 00:00:12,262
Uh, if anyone looks
like someone, <i>you</i> look like me.

4
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:14,598
<i>Like everyone else,
I believed that</i>

5
00:00:14,723 --> 00:00:16,641
<i>if the Avatar came back,
there would be bloodshed</i>

6
00:00:16,642 --> 00:00:18,935
<i>and destruction, but now...</i>

7
00:00:18,936 --> 00:00:20,771
<i>...I don't know.</i>

8
00:00:20,896 --> 00:00:23,106
By the Havens.

9
00:00:36,286 --> 00:00:38,080
<i>Fire.</i>

10
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:39,872
<i>Air.</i>

11
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:41,208
<i>Water.</i>

12
00:00:41,792 --> 00:00:42,876
<i>Earth.</i>

13
00:00:43,877 --> 00:00:48,339
<i>Long ago, the Avatar,
master of all four elements,</i>

14
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:50,633
<i>brought forth the Cataclysm.</i>

15
00:00:50,634 --> 00:00:52,343
<i>Out of the devastation,</i>

16
00:00:52,344 --> 00:00:55,097
<i>the world built
The Seven Havens.</i>

17
00:00:55,222 --> 00:00:57,182
<i>Now the Avatar has returned,</i>

18
00:00:57,307 --> 00:01:00,561
<i>but for the first time,
there are two.</i>

19
00:01:00,686 --> 00:01:03,062
<i>Most fear they'll destroy
the world again,</i>

20
00:01:03,063 --> 00:01:06,275
<i>but I believe
they will save it.</i>

21
00:01:24,209 --> 00:01:26,295
Who goes it?!

22
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:27,837
Good morning.

23
00:01:27,838 --> 00:01:29,672
It's just me and my kalimba.

24
00:01:36,221 --> 00:01:38,222
What are you doing with that?

25
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:40,559
My mind's been racing
since the storm,

26
00:01:40,684 --> 00:01:43,728
after that scary energy thing
zapped us.

27
00:01:43,729 --> 00:01:46,648
There's been this song
in the back of my mind.

28
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:49,233
Like a fuzzy memory.

29
00:01:49,234 --> 00:01:51,194
I think I've heard it before.

30
00:01:51,653 --> 00:01:53,864
It goes like...

31
00:01:59,911 --> 00:02:01,621
That's... lovely?

32
00:02:01,622 --> 00:02:05,625
Thanks. I do a lot of concerts
for my friends back home.

33
00:02:05,626 --> 00:02:06,668
Friends?

34
00:02:06,793 --> 00:02:08,044
I thought you were pretty much

35
00:02:08,169 --> 00:02:10,004
on your own, like me.

36
00:02:10,005 --> 00:02:12,465
I have loads of friends.

37
00:02:12,466 --> 00:02:14,467
You can't be totally alone.

38
00:02:14,468 --> 00:02:17,345
Wait, did you...
did you sleep on the ground?

39
00:02:17,346 --> 00:02:19,555
Of course! It's the best!

40
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:22,350
All the smells, the bugs,

41
00:02:22,351 --> 00:02:24,227
the weird mold.

42
00:02:24,353 --> 00:02:26,687
Not as great as my home.

43
00:02:26,688 --> 00:02:28,064
I miss the musk.

44
00:02:28,065 --> 00:02:31,025
Yeah, I know,
but this is your home now.

45
00:02:35,781 --> 00:02:37,699
Home? Huh.

46
00:02:37,824 --> 00:02:39,284
I guess you're right.

47
00:02:44,247 --> 00:02:46,708
How long will it
take to fix our home?

48
00:02:46,833 --> 00:02:48,418
I don't know, sweetie.

49
00:02:55,008 --> 00:02:56,550
Sleep well?

50
00:02:56,551 --> 00:02:59,763
I don't think
I'll ever sleep well again.

51
00:02:59,888 --> 00:03:01,347
Join the club.

52
00:03:01,348 --> 00:03:04,266
Are Pavi and Nisha okay?
I couldn't see what happened.

53
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:06,477
You're worried
about the Avatars?

54
00:03:06,478 --> 00:03:08,814
I-I don't...
That's not what I said.

55
00:03:08,939 --> 00:03:11,566
Law 47, Section One
of the Elloran Code states,

56
00:03:11,692 --> 00:03:13,651
you must report
any suspicious activity

57
00:03:13,652 --> 00:03:16,404
relating to the Avatar
to the council.

58
00:03:16,405 --> 00:03:19,156
The people need to know
the truth, right?

59
00:03:19,157 --> 00:03:22,202
You know why people <i>think</i>
they should know the truth?

60
00:03:22,327 --> 00:03:24,705
They believe
it'll keep them safe.

61
00:03:24,830 --> 00:03:29,126
Funny.
Usually the opposite is true.

62
00:03:29,251 --> 00:03:30,751
Do you trust me, Jae?

63
00:03:30,752 --> 00:03:31,837
Of course, sir.

64
00:03:31,962 --> 00:03:34,798
forget what you saw.

65
00:03:34,923 --> 00:03:37,675
You've got friends,
someone you love,

66
00:03:37,676 --> 00:03:40,594
a life
that you're comfortable with.

67
00:03:40,595 --> 00:03:41,888
Go back to it.

68
00:03:42,389 --> 00:03:43,807
I have a duty to Ellora.

69
00:03:43,932 --> 00:03:45,809
I need to tell the council
what I know.

70
00:03:46,309 --> 00:03:48,310
So be it.
First door on your left.

71
00:03:48,311 --> 00:03:49,979
Councilman Vinh's
a bit hard of hearing,

72
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:51,606
so you'll need to speak up.

73
00:03:52,566 --> 00:03:54,316
There will be consequences,
of course.

74
00:03:54,317 --> 00:03:57,903
I'll probably be imprisoned,
the girls will be exiled,

75
00:03:57,904 --> 00:04:01,240
left to fend for themselves
in the Harshlands.

76
00:04:01,241 --> 00:04:02,951
Or worse.

77
00:04:05,036 --> 00:04:07,747
Ellora has weathered
many storms,

78
00:04:07,748 --> 00:04:10,459
but nothing like
what we faced recently.

79
00:04:10,584 --> 00:04:11,835
We do not know much

80
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:14,587
about the strange energy
that attacked us,

81
00:04:14,588 --> 00:04:18,590
but I do know our haven
stands strong this day

82
00:04:18,591 --> 00:04:22,179
thanks to the incredible bravery
of our Bending Brigade.

83
00:04:22,929 --> 00:04:26,599
Captain Karthik,
with Commander Bountan injured,

84
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:29,019
our home needs you
more than ever.

85
00:04:31,104 --> 00:04:32,855
Speak freely, Jae.

86
00:04:32,856 --> 00:04:35,317
Your thoughts are valued
by the council.

87
00:04:35,776 --> 00:04:37,152
Um...

88
00:04:39,112 --> 00:04:40,946
The commander is...

89
00:04:40,947 --> 00:04:43,700
devoted to protecting Ellora.

90
00:04:44,493 --> 00:04:48,788
Captain Karthik, do you swear
to protect Ellora

91
00:04:48,789 --> 00:04:51,290
and keep true to the tenets
of our haven?

92
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:54,084
I serve at the will
of the council.

93
00:04:54,085 --> 00:04:56,630
The brigade is yours to lead.

94
00:04:57,005 --> 00:04:58,881
Keep us safe, Commander.

95
00:05:06,056 --> 00:05:09,391
Very well.
Thank you all for your service.

96
00:05:09,392 --> 00:05:12,229
Report to Tala to assist
with haven repairs.

97
00:05:15,941 --> 00:05:17,900
<i>Commander</i> Karthik.

98
00:05:17,901 --> 00:05:19,152
Stop it.

99
00:05:19,277 --> 00:05:20,362
You were the one destined

100
00:05:20,487 --> 00:05:22,404
for titles and banquets, not me.

101
00:05:22,405 --> 00:05:24,573
True.

102
00:05:24,574 --> 00:05:27,243
How you even got to captain
is a mystery.

103
00:05:27,244 --> 00:05:29,788
Did you ever make it on time
to a class?

104
00:05:29,913 --> 00:05:32,249
Once. At least.

105
00:05:33,124 --> 00:05:35,752
Kayoko, this energy Anomaly,

106
00:05:36,419 --> 00:05:38,712
we need reinforcements.

107
00:05:38,713 --> 00:05:41,383
Let's reach out to the other
havens for more benders.

108
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:44,802
And expose
the Haven's weaknesses?

109
00:05:44,803 --> 00:05:46,762
The council would never do that.

110
00:05:46,763 --> 00:05:49,099
You'll have to rely
on the benders you have.

111
00:05:49,516 --> 00:05:52,269
Asking for help isn't weak.
Please?

112
00:05:52,936 --> 00:05:55,313
They'll listen to you,
Chancellor.

113
00:05:57,232 --> 00:05:58,983
We're Ellorans, Karthik.

114
00:05:58,984 --> 00:06:01,069
We know how to take care
of ourselves.

115
00:06:01,486 --> 00:06:04,906
May the winds
always bend to you... Commander.

116
00:06:10,328 --> 00:06:13,665
Grab those!

117
00:06:13,790 --> 00:06:16,293
The council wants this gate
repaired immediately.

118
00:06:17,586 --> 00:06:21,214
Is the hardest working crew
in all of Ellora ready for...

119
00:06:21,339 --> 00:06:22,256
Pa-pa!

120
00:06:22,257 --> 00:06:23,049
...Kachoris!

121
00:06:24,384 --> 00:06:25,968
Fresh from Agam's snack shop.

122
00:06:25,969 --> 00:06:29,305
Mm! This is divine! Mmm!

123
00:06:29,306 --> 00:06:30,556
Mm-mm!

124
00:06:30,557 --> 00:06:33,435
A little thank you for working
a double shift.

125
00:06:34,185 --> 00:06:37,480
Hmm, I'll sleep a lot easier
once the gate is repaired.

126
00:06:37,606 --> 00:06:38,732
Yeah, uh...

127
00:06:38,857 --> 00:06:40,734
Not much this fancy
new gate can do

128
00:06:40,859 --> 00:06:43,402
since that zappy thing
came from underneath us.

129
00:06:43,403 --> 00:06:45,738
But it'll make people think
they're safe.

130
00:06:45,739 --> 00:06:47,073
And isn't that nice?

131
00:06:49,492 --> 00:06:51,076
Huh? Wh-what?

132
00:06:51,077 --> 00:06:53,454
You seemed distracted earlier.

133
00:06:53,455 --> 00:06:54,705
Are you okay?

134
00:06:54,706 --> 00:06:56,291
Datu?

135
00:06:56,416 --> 00:06:58,001
I need to tell you something.

136
00:06:59,794 --> 00:07:01,880
You know
you can tell me anything.

137
00:07:02,297 --> 00:07:04,132
It's about the Avatar. I--

138
00:07:04,257 --> 00:07:06,301
Oh, the festival, right?

139
00:07:06,426 --> 00:07:08,511
"Remember when the Avatar
destroyed the world,

140
00:07:08,637 --> 00:07:10,972
yadda, yadda, ya...
Eat lotus fritters."

141
00:07:12,307 --> 00:07:13,725
Whoa, whoa, whoa, wait.

142
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:16,686
Don't tell me
you actually had fun.

143
00:07:16,811 --> 00:07:18,563
No, no, it's...

144
00:07:18,939 --> 00:07:20,774
What if the Avatar
did come back?

145
00:07:21,483 --> 00:07:23,902
And she... or <i>he</i>

146
00:07:24,027 --> 00:07:26,528
wasn't horrible?

147
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:29,282
- What would you do?
- I'd protect my haven

148
00:07:29,407 --> 00:07:31,784
and kick the Avatar
out into the Harshlands.

149
00:07:31,785 --> 00:07:33,410
They're the reason
we live like this:

150
00:07:33,411 --> 00:07:34,913
isolated and afraid.

151
00:07:40,835 --> 00:07:43,505
Oh! Easy there!

152
00:07:43,630 --> 00:07:45,840
They've all been agitated
ever since the storm.

153
00:07:46,341 --> 00:07:48,718
You're okay.
We're here to protect you.

154
00:08:16,955 --> 00:08:19,582
What is this place?

155
00:08:22,502 --> 00:08:24,003
Hi!

156
00:08:24,004 --> 00:08:26,006
Is this your secret basement?

157
00:08:26,589 --> 00:08:28,133
You shouldn't be here!

158
00:08:36,057 --> 00:08:38,183
Wa-wait, Shilpa!
We're coworkers!

159
00:08:46,192 --> 00:08:47,985
Sorry, sorry. I'm <i>so</i> sorry!

160
00:08:47,986 --> 00:08:49,821
This is all
a big misunderstanding.

161
00:08:49,946 --> 00:08:51,698
Get back here!

162
00:08:58,371 --> 00:09:00,373
Hi.

163
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:03,292
I told you
to walk away.

164
00:09:03,293 --> 00:09:04,668
I suppose I should be proud

165
00:09:04,669 --> 00:09:07,255
I trained such an annoyingly
persistent bender.

166
00:09:08,173 --> 00:09:09,965
The Avatar saved me

167
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:12,217
and now you want me to, what,
lie forever

168
00:09:12,218 --> 00:09:14,053
and forget I saw any of that?

169
00:09:14,054 --> 00:09:16,056
We can burn those memories out!

170
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:21,560
Alright, Jae.

171
00:09:21,561 --> 00:09:23,063
What do you propose?

172
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:26,691
I'm confused, I'm scared,
I can't sleep,

173
00:09:26,816 --> 00:09:28,776
and I hate telling lies.

174
00:09:28,777 --> 00:09:30,319
It makes my ears itch.

175
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:33,198
Part of me wishes I'd never
followed you down here.

176
00:09:33,656 --> 00:09:37,827
But another part
wants to help those girls.

177
00:09:38,703 --> 00:09:41,246
What do you know
of the Order of the White Lotus?

178
00:09:41,247 --> 00:09:42,999
Uh--

179
00:09:43,124 --> 00:09:45,292
Uh, I've heard stories.

180
00:09:45,293 --> 00:09:47,377
A freaky underground cult

181
00:09:47,378 --> 00:09:50,131
that worships the Avatars...

182
00:09:50,256 --> 00:09:52,466
Oh!

183
00:09:52,467 --> 00:09:55,470
It's best if you come with me.

184
00:09:57,472 --> 00:09:59,933
We're not a cult, are we?

185
00:10:00,058 --> 00:10:01,434
Hmm.

186
00:10:04,187 --> 00:10:07,649
For ages, the White Lotus has
been working from the shadows

187
00:10:07,774 --> 00:10:10,151
to protect and train the Avatar.

188
00:10:11,486 --> 00:10:14,322
After the Cataclysm
two centuries ago,

189
00:10:14,447 --> 00:10:17,325
our numbers dwindled
to almost nothing.

190
00:10:20,203 --> 00:10:21,620
It's not easy.

191
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:24,707
Especially when the whole world
is against the Avatar.

192
00:10:25,083 --> 00:10:28,585
We need the Avatars
to mend our broken world

193
00:10:28,586 --> 00:10:30,796
but right now, they need us

194
00:10:30,797 --> 00:10:33,340
to teach them,
to protect their secret,

195
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:34,633
to help them.

196
00:10:34,634 --> 00:10:38,513
No one can know. Not your squad,

197
00:10:38,638 --> 00:10:40,305
not your loved ones.

198
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:42,724
Are you trying to scare me off?

199
00:10:42,725 --> 00:10:44,810
Is it working?

200
00:10:44,811 --> 00:10:46,312
I meant it earlier.

201
00:10:46,437 --> 00:10:48,606
You've got a good life, Jae.

202
00:10:48,731 --> 00:10:49,941
Think on it.

203
00:10:50,066 --> 00:10:52,818
And in the meantime,
you are welcome to observe.

204
00:10:52,819 --> 00:10:55,697
Just don't get in Hamka's way.

205
00:10:58,032 --> 00:11:01,202
Easy, easy, girl!
What's gotten into you?

206
00:11:06,124 --> 00:11:10,170
Yeah, you won't
believe that he said that.

207
00:11:14,257 --> 00:11:16,217
Uh...

208
00:11:17,719 --> 00:11:18,887
So...

209
00:11:19,012 --> 00:11:21,013
Is there like a chore chart or--

210
00:11:21,014 --> 00:11:22,806
- Shush!
- No? Okay.

211
00:11:26,603 --> 00:11:29,063
While you both were born
natural earthbenders,

212
00:11:29,189 --> 00:11:32,317
as Avatars, you must master
all the elements.

213
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:38,030
Nisha, show your sister
what you know.

214
00:11:57,383 --> 00:11:59,969
Try breathing out
with the movement

215
00:12:00,094 --> 00:12:01,303
instead of against it.

216
00:12:01,304 --> 00:12:03,973
I know how to breathe!

217
00:12:13,107 --> 00:12:15,068
Woo!

218
00:12:15,652 --> 00:12:17,487
Uh...

219
00:12:22,033 --> 00:12:23,451
Well done, Nisha!

220
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:25,827
Now then, Pavi?

221
00:12:25,828 --> 00:12:27,080
Oh, me?

222
00:12:27,205 --> 00:12:28,456
Do that?

223
00:12:28,581 --> 00:12:31,250
Nah, I'm-I'm not a...

224
00:12:36,297 --> 00:12:39,925
Ah! My eye!

225
00:12:39,926 --> 00:12:41,803
...kinda kid.

226
00:12:41,928 --> 00:12:44,681
Don't worry. It's just practice.

227
00:12:47,475 --> 00:12:50,352
Let go of me!
I'm not gonna fight anyone!

228
00:12:50,353 --> 00:12:51,771
Even for pretend.

229
00:12:52,355 --> 00:12:55,233
We are the Avatars.
We have to know how to fight.

230
00:12:55,358 --> 00:12:59,194
Why? Fighting only leads
to more fighting.

231
00:12:59,195 --> 00:13:00,195
What's the point?

232
00:13:01,322 --> 00:13:03,032
Hey, it's okay.

233
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:05,702
If she doesn't wanna fight,
she doesn't wanna fight.

234
00:13:05,827 --> 00:13:06,995
Who asked you?!

235
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:09,788
I just want to get to know
my sister.

236
00:13:09,789 --> 00:13:12,624
I don't care about being
the Avatar.

237
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:14,459
Oh, so then you don't care
about me?

238
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:16,253
I didn't say that!

239
00:13:16,254 --> 00:13:17,296
You might as well!

240
00:13:17,297 --> 00:13:19,507
Now, girls, let's not get upset.

241
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:21,008
We're not upset!

242
00:13:21,009 --> 00:13:22,677
And I don't care
about you either.

243
00:13:22,802 --> 00:13:26,514
Who wants to hang out with a
weirdo mold-missing musk lover?

244
00:13:26,639 --> 00:13:29,224
Let's take a break.

245
00:13:29,225 --> 00:13:31,144
I should've never come here.

246
00:13:31,686 --> 00:13:33,186
Then just leave!

247
00:13:33,187 --> 00:13:35,356
Go back
to all your cool friends!

248
00:13:35,773 --> 00:13:37,316
Fine! Maybe I will!

249
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:43,697
Nisha, go apologize.

250
00:13:43,698 --> 00:13:46,784
- But--
- Get your sister now!

251
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:52,707
What are we supposed to do
with them?

252
00:13:52,832 --> 00:13:54,625
Nisha's style has always
been chaotic,

253
00:13:54,751 --> 00:13:57,085
but the other one,
she's approximately...

254
00:13:57,086 --> 00:13:59,589
986 days and four hours behind
in training.

255
00:13:59,714 --> 00:14:01,883
If she won't fight,
what good is she?

256
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:04,135
We teach her.

257
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:05,594
This is an opportunity.

258
00:14:05,595 --> 00:14:07,929
There have never been
two Avatars at once.

259
00:14:07,930 --> 00:14:10,558
Together, they are the key
to fighting this Anomaly.

260
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:11,642
I know it.

261
00:14:11,768 --> 00:14:13,143
Jae?

262
00:14:13,144 --> 00:14:14,686
How am I supposed to help them

263
00:14:14,687 --> 00:14:16,396
when they won't listen to me?

264
00:14:16,397 --> 00:14:17,357
It's just...

265
00:14:17,482 --> 00:14:19,858
Gah!
This is so much responsibility!

266
00:14:19,859 --> 00:14:21,194
And risk!

267
00:14:21,944 --> 00:14:23,738
I am not cut out for this.

268
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:25,822
I know this is bigger
than anything

269
00:14:25,823 --> 00:14:27,325
you've taken on in the brigade.

270
00:14:27,450 --> 00:14:30,036
Responsibility is scary.

271
00:14:30,161 --> 00:14:32,079
It's a lot for people
to need you.

272
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:35,249
But all I'm asking for now
is for you to be Jae.

273
00:14:35,958 --> 00:14:37,377
A bender with heart.

274
00:14:37,502 --> 00:14:38,710
She left!

275
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:42,965
Pavi's gone.

276
00:14:45,009 --> 00:14:46,426
She left!

277
00:14:46,427 --> 00:14:49,596
I turned a corner and saw her
slip out a window with Geet!

278
00:14:49,597 --> 00:14:51,140
It's okay.

279
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:52,308
She can't have gone far.

280
00:14:52,433 --> 00:14:53,892
Let me find her.

281
00:14:53,893 --> 00:14:56,269
Send us, not the kid.

282
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:58,481
Commander, please,
I think I can get through to her

283
00:14:58,606 --> 00:15:00,023
if you let me.

284
00:15:00,024 --> 00:15:01,233
I've done it before.

285
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:09,575
He gets 7.85 minutes.

286
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:12,703
Yeah, then we follow him
to make sure he doesn't talk.

287
00:15:12,829 --> 00:15:15,373
No. I trust him.

288
00:15:21,754 --> 00:15:24,590
So, where are we going first?

289
00:15:25,007 --> 00:15:26,925
Are you allowed to be here?

290
00:15:26,926 --> 00:15:30,012
Karthik was right.
You're all about the rules.

291
00:15:30,638 --> 00:15:33,932
Really? Wha-what else did he say
about me?

292
00:15:37,520 --> 00:15:39,647
I chased her through here
a couple days ago.

293
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:41,356
I wonder if she lives nearby.

294
00:15:45,069 --> 00:15:46,154
Watch out!

295
00:15:49,073 --> 00:15:51,909
Hey, hey. All friends here. Hey.

296
00:15:52,034 --> 00:15:53,786
Its eyes.

297
00:15:54,412 --> 00:15:55,704
Something's wrong.

298
00:15:58,082 --> 00:15:59,750
Whoa, you gotta teach me that.

299
00:16:30,323 --> 00:16:31,866
Let me handle this.

300
00:17:03,814 --> 00:17:05,774
We have to stop scaring it.

301
00:17:05,775 --> 00:17:09,277
Please, just let me
try something.

302
00:17:19,372 --> 00:17:21,332
It's okay.

303
00:17:21,457 --> 00:17:22,958
You're scared.

304
00:17:22,959 --> 00:17:24,752
Like me, right?

305
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:01,872
Mom?

306
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:05,167
That song.

307
00:18:06,127 --> 00:18:07,837
I remember.

308
00:18:07,962 --> 00:18:12,132
She wore her hair
just like yours,

309
00:18:12,133 --> 00:18:13,509
I can teach you.

310
00:18:14,093 --> 00:18:15,469
If you want.

311
00:18:15,970 --> 00:18:18,346
I'm sorry about before.

312
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:19,932
Me too.

313
00:18:20,057 --> 00:18:22,351
Could I meet your friends?

314
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:27,773
There you are!

315
00:18:27,898 --> 00:18:31,359
Luster and Mica,
this is my sister.

316
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:32,403
Huh?

317
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:36,240
Oh! <i>These</i> are your friends!

318
00:18:38,284 --> 00:18:40,952
It's not much, but it's home.

319
00:18:40,953 --> 00:18:42,705
Or it was.

320
00:18:43,289 --> 00:18:46,541
I like sleeping
on the ground,

321
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:49,420
talking to bugs,
playing my kalimba.

322
00:18:50,838 --> 00:18:52,964
I want to stay with you,

323
00:18:52,965 --> 00:18:55,467
but I don't wanna stop being me.

324
00:18:55,468 --> 00:18:58,929
And I wanna know the real you.

325
00:18:59,472 --> 00:19:01,390
Rock friends and all.

326
00:19:06,062 --> 00:19:07,813
Sorry! Sorry.

327
00:19:07,938 --> 00:19:11,317
Your guards...
I mean, guardians.

328
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:15,905
What if I'm not what they expect
an Avatar to be like?

329
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:17,448
Karthik's been there for me.

330
00:19:17,573 --> 00:19:19,617
He'll be there for you too.
I know it.

331
00:19:20,159 --> 00:19:22,327
Responsibility can be scary.

332
00:19:22,328 --> 00:19:24,205
It's a lot for people
to need you.

333
00:19:24,330 --> 00:19:28,084
But all you need to be right now
is Pavi.

334
00:19:28,209 --> 00:19:29,501
That's plenty.

335
00:19:29,502 --> 00:19:32,672
And you won't have
to do it alone

336
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:36,091
'cause I'll be right there
with you.

337
00:19:36,092 --> 00:19:38,385
And so will Nisha, right?

338
00:19:38,386 --> 00:19:42,098
Yup, and we can be the kind
of Avatars we wanna be.

339
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:45,893
Pack your bags.

340
00:19:46,268 --> 00:19:48,436
It's moving day!

341
00:19:55,361 --> 00:19:56,528
Jae!

342
00:19:56,529 --> 00:19:59,532
Datu! What are you doing here?

343
00:19:59,657 --> 00:20:02,784
Hey, I've been looking
all over for you and...

344
00:20:02,785 --> 00:20:04,537
Oh, hi!

345
00:20:04,662 --> 00:20:06,580
Who are these little ones?

346
00:20:06,706 --> 00:20:08,456
Uh, they're friends.

347
00:20:08,457 --> 00:20:11,960
Family! Family friends.

348
00:20:11,961 --> 00:20:14,462
Touch the hair, lose your hand.

349
00:20:16,716 --> 00:20:19,385
Little rascal!
Anyway, I've gotta run.

350
00:20:19,510 --> 00:20:21,010
Important brigade business.

351
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:22,471
See you later, okay?

352
00:20:28,894 --> 00:20:32,314
Commander Karthik,
I'm really sorry for leaving.

353
00:20:32,815 --> 00:20:34,649
I brought some friends back.

354
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:36,193
I'll introduce you later.

355
00:20:36,736 --> 00:20:39,280
And I want to ask you
for a favor.

356
00:20:39,905 --> 00:20:41,657
I thought my parents were gone,

357
00:20:41,782 --> 00:20:43,576
but then I found Nisha.

358
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:45,536
So...

359
00:20:47,496 --> 00:20:49,999
...maybe our mom and dad
are still out there too.

360
00:20:50,124 --> 00:20:52,834
Do you think you can help us
find them?

361
00:20:52,835 --> 00:20:54,962
I give you my word.

362
00:20:56,297 --> 00:20:58,090
Also...

363
00:20:58,591 --> 00:21:00,592
We want Jae to teach us.

364
00:21:00,593 --> 00:21:03,304
I'm ready. I won't let you down.

365
00:21:05,473 --> 00:21:07,266
Welcome to the Order.

366
00:21:13,314 --> 00:21:14,940
There goes my sweets fund.

367
00:21:15,065 --> 00:21:17,526
Always bet on airbenders
doing the right thing.

368
00:21:17,651 --> 00:21:20,528
Oh! Can you teach me how to use
your air skimmer?

369
00:21:20,529 --> 00:21:21,946
Well...

370
00:21:21,947 --> 00:21:24,199
I dunno, it's pretty advanced.

371
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:25,951
Yeah, we're the Avatars.

372
00:21:26,076 --> 00:21:27,703
I think we can handle it.

373
00:21:32,124 --> 00:21:35,294
Wait!

374
00:21:36,128 --> 00:21:38,379
You girls are gonna be
the death of me.

375
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:41,008
Relax, wind boy, we got this.

376
00:21:42,259 --> 00:21:43,718
Oof!

377
00:21:45,054 --> 00:21:47,138
Okay, we've got
some stuff to learn,

378
00:21:47,139 --> 00:21:49,641
but Ellora now has two Avatars.

379
00:21:49,642 --> 00:21:52,519
We can take care of whatever
comes our way!

